        "note": "Companion formalisation by the same maintainer, registered in the Palomar registry as PALOMAR-2026-09-25-000023 (commit 2ae1bccb82f1f72ed7a7aeab3196aa1cdbee165a): at least one of ζ₂(7), ζ₂(9), ζ₂(11) is irrational, by a different construction. The theorem recorded here implies it. This repository started as a copy of that one and reuses its infrastructure unchanged: the six trusted definitions (identical, so both statements are about the same zeta2), the statements and proofs of the convergence of J s, the translation formula, Lai's criterion and the Δ-calculus (Zeta2Lean/Proofs, files identical to those of that commit), and the proof of the prime number theorem (Zeta2Lean/Cited: identical vendored files, and PNT.lean, which collects that repository's PNT statements and proofs in one file). The construction, the denominator and growth bounds and the nonvanishing argument are new here.",
